# Pretty addresses for journal entries: /journal/orion-nebula-in-binoculars is answered by
# post.html, which reads the slug from the address. A rewrite (200), so the URL stays put.
#
# from          to            status
/journal/*      /post.html    200

# The pages link to each other without .html (/journal, /studio): the host answers /journal with
# journal.html by itself. These send the old .html addresses on to the clean ones. The ! applies a
# rule even though the file exists, which is the point here; a rule only ever sees the address
# asked for, so /journal, answered by journal.html, is never sent round again.
/index.html     /             301!
/*.html         /:1           301!

# Everything else that is not a real page gets the "Lost in space" page and an honest 404,
# instead of the home page the host would fall back to for a single-page app.
/**             /404.html     404
